<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fujiwara no Kiyohira</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1056–<a href="/years/1128">1128</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fujiwara no Kiyohira was the founder of the Northern Fujiwara of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. The son of a Fujiwara father killed in the Former Nine Years' War, he was raised in the Kiyohara family, and after the Later Three Years' War of 1083 to 1087 he became master of Mutsu and Dewa. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiraizumi">Hiraizumi</a> his seat and built it up with temples such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chuson-ji">Chūson-ji</a>, and his remains lie in its Golden Hall.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fujiwara-no-kiyohira.jpg" alt="Fujiwara no Kiyohira" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fujiwara_no_Kiyohira.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
